<script type="module" is:inline>
  import twemoji from "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/twemoji@14.0.2/+esm";
  window.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {
    twemoji.parse(document.body, {
      folder: "svg",
      ext: ".svg"
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  /* Import Noto Color Emoji font (you might not need this if only using Twemoji) */
  @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Color+Emoji&display=swap');

  /* Style for the container of the Twemoji SVG */
  .twemoji {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    width: 100%; /* Ensure the container takes full width */
    height: auto; /* Adjust height automatically based on content */
  }

  /* Style the Twemoji SVG image */
  .twemoji img {
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
    max-width: 100%; /* Make it responsive within its container */
    max-height: 160px; /* Set a reasonable maximum size */
    object-fit: contain; /* Maintain aspect ratio */
  }

  .turnpike-button {
    font-family: 'Highway Gothic', Arial, sans-serif;
    background-color: #005f25;
    color: #ffd700;
    border: 4px solid #ffd700;
    border-radius: 0;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: all 0.3s ease;
    letter-spacing: 1.5px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2);
  }

  .turnpike-button:hover {
    background-color: #004a1c;
    color: #ffea66;
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 6px 12px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
  }

  /* Force emoji size (you likely don't need this anymore) */
  /* .twemoji img {
    max-height: 400px;
  } */

  /* Make sure large emojis are visible and responsive (adjust max-width) */
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .twemoji img {
      max-width: 80px; /* Adjust for smaller screens */
    }
  }
</style>

**Key Changes:**

1.  **Removed `emoji-*` CSS Rules:** The entire block of CSS defining `.emoji-TV::before`, `.emoji-Tree::before`, etc., has been removed. This was the source of the fixed large emoji size.
2.  **Updated HTML:** The `<span>` tag displaying the emoji now has the class `twemoji` instead of `emoji-${service.emoji}`. Twemoji will target elements with this class to replace the text emoji with an SVG.
3.  **Simplified CSS:** The remaining CSS focuses on styling the container of the Twemoji SVG (`.twemoji`) and the Twemoji SVG image itself (`.twemoji img`) to control its size and responsiveness.
4.  **Adjusted `max-height`:** The `max-height` for `.twemoji img` is set to `160px` initially, and then adjusted for smaller screens in the media query. You can adjust these values to your desired size.

By making these changes, you'll be relying on the Twemoji script to handle the rendering and sizing of your emojis, ensuring they scale properly and don't appear excessively large.
